 Top Docker, K8s & Helm Commands for DevOps Interview Preparation 🚀

If you’re preparing for DevOps interviews, mastering these core commands will help you stand out in practical rounds. 💪

🐳 Docker – Most Used Commands
docker ps → List running containers
docker images → Show all available images
docker build -t myapp . → Build Docker image
docker run -d -p 8080:80 myapp → Run container in background
docker exec -it <container> bash → Access running container shell
docker logs <container> → View container logs
docker rm -f <container> → Remove container
docker rmi <image> → Remove image
docker-compose up -d → Start multiple services
docker network ls / docker volume ls → Manage networks & volumes

☸️ Kubernetes (kubectl) – Daily Used Commands
kubectl get pods / kubectl get all → View resources
kubectl describe pod <name> → Detailed info of pod
kubectl logs <pod> → Check pod logs
kubectl exec -it <pod> -- bash → Access container shell
kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml → Apply changes
kubectl delete -f deployment.yaml → Delete resources
kubectl get nodes → List all cluster nodes
kubectl rollout status deployment/<name> → Check rollout progress
kubectl scale deployment <name> --replicas=3 → Scale apps
kubectl port-forward pod/<name> 8080:80 → Access service locally

🧭 Helm – Package Manager for Kubernetes
helm repo add stable https://lnkd.in/g7irxF5n → Add chart repo
helm repo update → Update repo
helm search repo nginx → Search chart
helm install my-nginx stable/nginx → Install chart
helm list → List all releases
helm upgrade my-nginx stable/nginx → Upgrade release
helm rollback my-nginx 1 → Rollback to version
helm uninstall my-nginx → Remove release
helm get values my-nginx → View release values
helm template my-nginx . → Render manifests locally

🎯 Pro Tip
👉 Practice these commands hands-on using Minikube / Kind (for K8s) and Docker Desktop.
 👉 Focus on real-time debugging, pod crashes, and deployment rollouts — common interview topics.
